the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    Credit worthiness check holds for *a case*.
    Income verification holds for *a case*; open textured.
    Credit score check holds for *a case*; open textured.

the knowledge base r3_4_credit_worthiness_check includes:

the text of the_rulemap is at "sources/credit-worthiness-check.ruml".

Credit worthiness check holds for a case if
    Income verification holds for the case
    and Credit score check holds for the case.

scenario generated_1 is, as stated in "credit-worthiness-check.ruml" at generated_1:
    % no data
    node_1 expects answers ["Credit worthiness check holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.
    not_node_1 expects answers ["it is not the case that Credit worthiness check holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.
    node_2 expects answers ["Income verification holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.
    not_node_2 expects answers ["it is not the case that Income verification holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.
    node_3 expects answers ["Credit score check holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.
    not_node_3 expects answers ["it is not the case that Credit score check holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.

query node_1 is:
    Credit worthiness check holds for case 1.

query not_node_1 is:
    it is not the case that Credit worthiness check holds for case 1.

query node_2 is:
    Income verification holds for case 1.

query not_node_2 is:
